========================================================================================
T4b  THE PHYSICALLY RELEVANT RANK: velocity rows only
========================================================================================
  A generalised FORCE is fixed by its three velocity-row components, and its
  position-row effect is the same O(Ts^2) integrator factor the baseline has (T3).
  So the pointwise question for a real addition is the rank of the 3 x 10 block.

  rank histogram (max 3): {3: 686}
  sigma_3 / sigma_1 per sample:
        0% quantile  5.7217e-04
        1% quantile  1.4323e-03
       50% quantile  1.3650e-02
      100% quantile  2.2888e-01

  T4b verdict: rank = 3 of 3 at 686 of 686 samples (100.00 %), worst conditioning 5.72e-04
  => the three logical force channels are spanned at EVERY sample, robustly.
     No nonzero pointwise-orthogonal FORCE exists. The no-go lemma holds for
     physically realisable additions, and with margin rather than marginally.

